{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSYBH5Eta7E9aQvddjkT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings** (in order of relevance):\n- `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — Current controller with POST /shipments (create), GET /shipments/{shipmentId}, GET /shipments endpoints\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` — ShipmentStatus enum: CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27` — InMemoryShipmentRepository: save(shipment), findById(id), existsById(id), findAll()\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:19-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) exceptions\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` — Converts ApiExceptions to ApiError responses using status and code\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler converts to HTTP responses\n2. ResourceNotFoundException maps to 404 with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` error code\n3. ConflictException maps to 409 with appropriate error codes\n4. Controllers return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(resource)` for POST operations\n5. Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions for both success and error cases\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — Must add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n2. `ErrorCode.kt` — Will likely need a new error code for \"shipment in invalid state\" (cannot confirm a CANCELLED shipment)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Must add tests for the new confirm endpoint behavior\n\n**Risks:**\n1. The repository doesn't have an update method; I'll use save() which should work with the concurrent map\n2. Need to handle idempotency: confirming already-CONFIRMED shipment must succeed\n3. Need to use correct HTTP status 409 for CANCELLED shipments\n4. Must not break existing tests\n\n**Open questions:**\n1. Should I add a new ErrorCode for \"shipment in invalid state\" or reuse SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS? The ticket says ConflictException (409) for CANCELLED, so I need an appropriate error code. Let me check if adding an ErrorCode counts as a \"new dependency\" or if it's just an enum value.\n\nBased on the constraints (\"Do not add new dependencies\" and \"No unrelated production file changes\"), adding an ErrorCode enum value should be acceptable since it's not a dependency but a simple enum constant.\n\nNow I'm ready for DESIGN.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ErrorCode.kt** — Add a new enum value `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to represent when a shipment cannot be confirmed due to its current status (e.g., CANCELLED).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a POST handler method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` that:\n   - Finds the shipment by ID; throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)\n   - If status is CREATED, updates it to CONFIRMED and saves it\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns it unchanged (idempotent success)\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException (409, SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n   - Returns the shipment in the response body with appropriate HTTP status (200 OK for both confirm-and-update and already-confirmed cases)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test cases:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` — POST confirm on CREATED, expect 200 and status=CONFIRMED\n   - `idempotently succeeds when confirming an already CONFIRMED shipment` — Create, confirm, confirm again, expect 200 both times with CONFIRMED status\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` — Set status to CANCELLED directly in repo, POST confirm, expect 409 with error code\n   - `reports unknown shipment with 404` — POST confirm on non-existent ID, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- I could make confirm() a service method in a separate ShipmentService class to separate concerns, but the existing codebase doesn't use a service layer (only controller and repository), so following the existing pattern is better for consistency.\n- I could reuse SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS for the CANCELLED error, but that would be semantically incorrect (the shipment exists, but is in the wrong state). Adding SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE is clearer.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Processing | Output | Status |\n|------|-------|------------|--------|--------|\n| Confirm CREATED | shipmentId exists, status=CREATED | Find shipment, update status to CONFIRMED, save | Shipment with status=CONFIRMED | 200 OK |\n| Confirm CONFIRMED | shipmentId exists, status=CONFIRMED | Find shipment, return unchanged | Shipment with status=CONFIRMED | 200 OK |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | shipmentId exists, status=CANCELLED | Find shipment, throw ConflictException | ApiError with code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE | 409 Conflict |\n| Confirm unknown | shipmentId does not exist | Throw ResourceNotFoundException | ApiError with code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND | 404 Not Found |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. Test idempotency: Create, confirm (200), confirm again (200), verify status unchanged\n2. Test state transition: Create, confirm (200), verify status changed to CONFIRMED\n3. Test invalid state: Manually insert CANCELLED shipment, confirm (409), verify error code\n4. Test not found: Confirm non-existent ID (404), verify error code\n5. Verify existing tests still pass (create, get by id, list, duplicate create rejection)\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1789,"cache_read_input_tokens":19113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1789},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_